# CODEOWNERS for exec-skills repo
# Requires the listed owner(s) to approve any PR touching that path.
# Enable in GitHub: Settings > Branches > Branch protection rule >
# "Require review from Code Owners" (this file must live at
# .github/CODEOWNERS, /CODEOWNERS, or /docs/CODEOWNERS in the repo root).

# Shared base template — changes here affect every role, require
# broader sign-off (e.g., Chief of Staff + General Counsel).
/_base/                 @chief-of-staff-github-handle @general-counsel-github-handle

# Per-role manifests — only that executive (or their named delegate)
# and the accountable governance function can approve changes.
/ceo/                   @ceo-github-handle @chief-of-staff-github-handle
/cto/                   @cto-github-handle @ciso-github-handle
/cpo/                   @cpo-github-handle @privacy-officer-github-handle
/clo/                   @clo-github-handle @general-counsel-github-handle

# CI/governance tooling itself — require security + legal sign-off
# since this controls how the lint/validation checks behave.
/.github/               @general-counsel-github-handle @ciso-github-handle

# Replace every @handle above with real GitHub usernames or team
# handles (e.g., @yourorg/legal-team) before enabling branch protection.
